	"img": "icons/weapons/axes/axe-double-jagged-black.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>The double crescent axe is known by many names in various cultures. The drek, for example, call it a mek’tar. The weapon’s shape is defined by a crescent shaped edge with forward curling blades at the ends nestled into a second, longer, crescent which also has forward curling blades at the ends. With the back of the larger curving crescent typically having hand-holds cut into it in at least two, but often three, places.</p><p>When wielded with the hands on grips on either side of the weapon, it functions as a weapon with the double weapon property and each end deals 1d6 damage. However if both hands are used on the same grip, it is instead treated as a versatile weapon dealing 1d10 damage.</p>",
